  "worked_solution": "To get the values of $x$ and $y$ in the second row, we add $\u0394x$ to $x$ and $\u0394y$ to $y,$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+\u0394x \\\\  & =4+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{4} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\u0394y \\\\  & =4+2 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these results to our table gives the following:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{\u2032}\\,$ | $\\,\u0394y\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $4$ | $8$ | $2$ |\n| $\\frac{17}{4}$ | $6$ | $$ | $$ |\n\nNext, we compute ${y}^{\u2032}$ according to the given rule (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the second row), and we compute \n$\u0394y$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{\u2032} & =x\\sqrt{y} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{6} \\\\ \u0394y & ={y}^{\u2032}\\cdot \u0394x \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{4}\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\sqrt{6}}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{\u2032}\\,$ | $\\,\u0394y\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $4$ | $8$ | $2$ |\n| $\\frac{17}{4}$ | $6$ | $\\frac{17}{4}\\sqrt{6}$ | $\\frac{17\\sqrt{6}}{16}$ |",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
